  What each trigger means:
    MKT_UNDER_US         the market's implied chance for our side is 10c below our model's
    MODEL_P10            the MODEL's chance we lose has reached 10% (the earlier study's rule, for comparison)
    MODEL_P50            the MODEL's chance we lose has reached 50% (the earlier study's rule, for comparison)
    MODEL_P90            the MODEL's chance we lose has reached 90% (the earlier study's rule, for comparison)
    MU_AND_SPOT          the projected settlement AND the index are both on the wrong side
    MU_CROSS             the projected settlement (locked prints + spot) has crossed K_eff -- arithmetic, no probability
    MU_CROSS_HOLD2       the projected settlement has been the wrong side of K_eff for 2 seconds running
    MU_CROSS_HOLD3       the projected settlement has been the wrong side of K_eff for 3 seconds running
    NEARLINE_T10_S10     at tau<=10s the index is within 1 sigma*sqrt(tau) of K_eff
    NEARLINE_T10_S5      at tau<=10s the index is within 0.5 sigma*sqrt(tau) of K_eff
    NEARLINE_T20_S10     at tau<=20s the index is within 1 sigma*sqrt(tau) of K_eff
    PRICE_DROP15         the market's bid for our side has fallen 15c below what we paid
    PRICE_DROP30         the market's bid for our side has fallen 30c below what we paid
    PRICE_DROP5          the market's bid for our side has fallen 5c below what we paid
    SPOT_CROSS           the index itself is on the wrong side of K_eff
    SPOT_CROSS_HOLD2     the index has been on the wrong side for 2 seconds running
    SPOT_CROSS_HOLD3     the index has been on the wrong side for 3 seconds running
    SPOT_CROSS_HOLD5     the index has been on the wrong side for 5 seconds running

